\begin{eqnarray*}
f(-x)-f(x) &=&\lfloor -x \rfloor +\frac{1}{2} -\lfloor -x \rfloor -\frac{1}{2}\\
&=&0
\end{eqnarray*}
<answer> The function is symmetric about the $$x$$ axis, therefore the function $$f(x) = \lfloor x \rfloor + \frac{1}{2}$$ is <answer> even</answer>

